Makes the two inference APIs of the Citadel gateway-upgrade module refuse a call that is not made with a contract's key.

A contract is a product with its own policy: the models the consumer may ask for and its tokens a minute and a month. A key
that is not tied to a product (the API Management instance's own all-access key, or a key for one API or for all APIs) never
runs the product's policy, so the models and the limits of the contracts would not apply to it. The kit lets such a call
through (its security handler names it "Portal-Admin"); this patch refuses it with 403 and the code contract_required, in
the policies of universal-llm-api and azure-openai-api, so an unlimited path to the models does not exist by accident. The
rule comes after the kit's security handler, so a call with no key or a wrong key still gets the handler's 401.

It applies to the kit at the commit that the workflows check out (Azure-Samples/ai-hub-gateway-solution-accelerator,
citadel-v1); the checks apply it for real, and the gateway run reads the two policies back from the instance. Calls with the
key of a contract are not affected.

diff --git a/bicep/infra/modules/apim/policies/universal-llm-api-policy-v2.xml b/bicep/infra/modules/apim/policies/universal-llm-api-policy-v2.xml
--- a/bicep/infra/modules/apim/policies/universal-llm-api-policy-v2.xml
+++ b/bicep/infra/modules/apim/policies/universal-llm-api-policy-v2.xml
@@ -26,2 +26,16 @@
         <!-- Step 2: Extract and validate model parameter from request -->
+        <!-- Meternaut: a call is answered only when it is made with the key of a contract (a subscription of a product). The
+             instance's own all-access key and any other key that is not tied to a product are refused: the contract's models
+             and token limits are in the product's policy and would not apply to them. -->
+        <choose>
+            <when condition="@(context.Product == null)">
+                <return-response>
+                    <set-status code="403" reason="Forbidden" />
+                    <set-header name="Content-Type" exists-action="override">
+                        <value>application/json</value>
+                    </set-header>
+                    <set-body>{"error":{"code":"contract_required","message":"This gateway answers only calls made with the key of a contract."}}</set-body>
+                </return-response>
+            </when>
+        </choose>
         <include-fragment fragment-id="set-llm-requested-model" />
